        why_en: "Polymerase ε makes the leading strand and polymerase δ the lagging strand, and both carry 3'→5' proofreading exonucleases. Polymerase α is a polymerase-primase: one subunit has the primase activity, the largest subunit (Mr ~180,000) the polymerase activity, and it lays down the RNA primer then extends it by about 10 nucleotides of DNA to start each Okazaki fragment. It explicitly has NO proofreading exonuclease, which makes it unsuitable for high-fidelity replication — hence the handover to δ or ε. PCNA is not a proofreading subunit at all: it is the sliding clamp, the structural counterpart of the E. coli β subunit despite the absence of evident sequence homology.",
        why_cn: "聚合酶ε合成先导链，聚合酶δ合成滞后链，两者都带有3′→5′校对外切核酸酶。聚合酶α是一种「聚合酶–引发酶」：其中一个亚基具有引发酶活性，最大的亚基（Mr约180,000）具有聚合酶活性；它先铺下RNA引物，再把它延伸约10个核苷酸的DNA，以启动每一个冈崎片段。书中明确指出它没有校对外切核酸酶活性，因此不适合高保真复制——这正是要交棒给δ或ε的原因。PCNA根本不是什么校对亚基：它是滑动夹子，尽管看不出明显的序列同源性，却是大肠杆菌β亚基在结构上的对应物。"
