        why_en: "The selectivity is built in twice, then reinforced by a third effect. First, activation: aciclovir is inert until phosphorylated, and the kinase that does it is virally encoded and binds the drug with 200-fold greater affinity than the cellular thymidine kinase, so acyclo-GMP is formed essentially only in infected cells. Cellular kinases then make acyclo-GTP. Second, the target: acyclo-GTP competitively inhibits the herpes polymerase more strongly than cellular polymerases. Third, because it consists of guanine on an incomplete ribose ring it lacks a 3'-OH, so once incorporated it acts as a chain terminator — the direct consequence of the rule that a polymerase can only extend from a free 3'-OH.",
        why_cn: "选择性是双重内建的，之后还被第三重效应强化。第一，活化：阿昔洛韦在被磷酸化之前是惰性的，而完成磷酸化的激酶由病毒编码，它结合该药物的亲和力比细胞胸苷激酶高200倍，所以acyclo-GMP基本上只在被感染的细胞里形成。随后由细胞激酶生成acyclo-GTP。第二，靶点：acyclo-GTP对疱疹病毒聚合酶的竞争性抑制强于对细胞聚合酶的抑制。第三，由于它是鸟嘌呤连在一个不完整的核糖环上，缺少3′-OH，所以一旦被掺入就充当链终止剂——这正是「聚合酶只能从游离的3′-OH往下延伸」这条规则的直接后果。"
